    paragraphs: [
      "BtechWaleTech is three engineers based in India. Ankur Kumar is a full stack developer who builds the front ends, back ends and integrations. Santosh Sharma works on AI and machine learning, AWS, data, technical SEO and deployment. Vedansh Shrivastava runs project delivery and works on data science, AI and automation. When a client in Japan messages us, one of those three people replies, and the same people write the code. There is no director or account manager in between and no hand-off to a subcontractor you never meet.",
      `We are not a Japanese company. We do not have an office in Japan, a registered ${ja("株式会社")} or ${ja("合同会社")}, local staff or a Google Business Profile with a Japanese address. Some offshore providers blur this with a virtual office in Shibuya or a rental desk in Minato; we would rather be plain about it. You are hiring a remote team in India, and the rest of this page explains how that works in practice, what it costs compared with Japanese agencies, and where it helps or does not help your business.`,
      "We also work in English, and that matters more in Japan than in most markets. Our team does not write natural Japanese and cannot run a meeting in keigo. We are the right fit for foreign-owned companies and their Japanese subsidiaries; international startups in Tokyo and Fukuoka; hotels, ryokan, tour operators and experience providers that need English, Chinese and Korean sites for inbound visitors; Japanese manufacturers and food producers selling abroad who need English sites and cross-border stores; bilingual professionals such as visa specialists, international real estate agents, English schools and international schools; and Japanese companies whose teams already work in English with overseas partners.",
      "If your team works only in Japanese, the project can still work well with one bilingual colleague or a translator in the loop. We write short, plain English messages that translation tools handle reliably, put every decision in writing, and use screenshots and staging links rather than long explanations. The Japanese text on your site is written or reviewed by a native speaker, never by us.",
      "The practical side is simple. A first conversation happens on WhatsApp, email or a video call. We write down what you need as a scope document, similar to a short requirements definition: pages, features, integrations, languages, who supplies content, what is excluded, and a timeline. You approve it before anything is billed. During the build you get a private staging link that you can open on your own phone at any time, so you review real pages rather than static mock-ups. Small changes usually land the same day because our working hours cover your afternoon and evening.",
      `Japan already relies heavily on outside engineering help. The Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry estimated that the country could be short of up to 790,000 IT workers by 2030, and offshore development (${ja("オフショア開発")}) to Vietnam, the Philippines, China and India is common. Where remote delivery is weaker, we say so: we cannot visit your shop to photograph products, attend a meeting in your office or sit with your staff while they learn a new admin panel. For photography we recommend a local photographer and tell you exactly which shots and sizes we need. For training we record short screen videos your staff can keep and replay.`,
    ],
