    paragraphs: [
      "This section describes the practical groundwork we build into websites for Japan. It is not legal or tax advice. We are engineers, not lawyers, and for formal questions you should speak to a qualified adviser in Japan.",
      `<strong>Act on the Protection of Personal Information (APPI).</strong> The APPI (${ja("個人情報保護法")}) governs how businesses handle personal information, and the Personal Information Protection Commission enforces it. Businesses must specify and publish the purposes for which they use personal information, keep it secure, and since the 2022 amendments report certain data breaches to the Commission and notify the people affected. We build forms that collect only the fields you need, link to a privacy policy that states purposes of use, store submissions in access-controlled systems and keep admin access role-based.`,
      "<strong>Providing data to a team in India.</strong> This is the point most offshore providers skip. Under the APPI, giving a contractor in a foreign country access to personal data counts as provision to a third party in a foreign country. It generally requires either the individual's consent, after being told the country and its data protection system, or a contractor with a protection system that meets the APPI's standards. India has the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, which is being phased in. We design projects so we rarely need live personal data at all, use dummy data for testing, keep production access minimal and sign data-handling terms, but your adviser should decide the basis your company relies on.",
      `<strong>Specified Commercial Transactions Act.</strong> Online stores are mail-order businesses under the Specified Commercial Transactions Act (${ja("特定商取引法")}) and must display a page with the seller's name, address and phone number, the person responsible, prices, shipping costs, payment methods and timing, delivery timing and the returns policy. Since June 2022 the final confirmation screen before an order must clearly show key terms such as quantity, price, payment, delivery and cancellation conditions, especially for subscriptions. We build that page and the confirmation screen into every Japanese store.`,
      `<strong>Misleading representations and stealth marketing.</strong> The Act against Unjustifiable Premiums and Misleading Representations (${ja("景品表示法")}) prohibits exaggerated quality claims and misleading prices, such as fake reference prices. Since October 2023 it also covers stealth marketing: advertising that hides the fact that it is advertising, such as undisclosed paid influencer posts, is prohibited. We avoid unverifiable superlatives and label sponsored content clearly.`,
      `<strong>Clinics, cosmetics and health products.</strong> Medical institution websites are regulated as advertising under the medical advertising guidelines (${ja("医療広告ガイドライン")}): patient testimonials about treatment are not allowed, and before-and-after photos need detailed explanations of the treatment, costs and risks. Cosmetics, supplements and health foods are restricted in what they can claim under the Pharmaceutical and Medical Device Act and related rules. We build pages that leave room for careful wording, and you or your adviser approve every claim.`,
      `<strong>Marketing email.</strong> The Act on Regulation of Transmission of Specified Electronic Mail (${ja("特定電子メール法")}) generally requires prior opt-in consent for marketing email, records of that consent, the sender's details and a working way to opt out. We set up newsletter tools with confirmed opt-in, consent records and proper unsubscribe handling.`,
      "<strong>External transmission rules.</strong> Since June 2023, the Telecommunications Business Act requires many online services to tell users what information is sent to third parties through tags and SDKs, such as analytics and advertising scripts. Simple corporate sites promoting your own business are generally outside the rule, but ecommerce platforms, apps and information services may be covered. If yours is in scope, we add a clear disclosure page listing each tool and what it receives.",
      "<strong>Consumption tax and the invoice system.</strong> Consumer prices must be shown including consumption tax, currently 10 percent with a reduced 8 percent rate for most food. Since October 2023, businesses that want customers to claim input tax credits must issue qualified invoices, and registered stores need invoice templates with their registration number. On our own invoices: we are an India-based provider and are not registered as a qualified invoice issuer in Japan, so we do not add Japanese consumption tax. How imported services are treated depends on the service and your company's position; your tax accountant will know.",
      "<strong>Accessibility.</strong> Japan's accessibility standard for websites is JIS X 8341-3, which is aligned with WCAG. Since April 2024, amendments to the Act for Eliminating Discrimination against Persons with Disabilities have made reasonable accommodation mandatory for private businesses. We build to WCAG 2.2 AA as a working standard: sufficient colour contrast, keyboard navigation, meaningful link text, alt text on images, labelled form fields and readable font sizes, which also helps Japan's large older population.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "time-zone",
    heading: "Working hours: Japan time and India time",
    paragraphs: [
      "Japan Standard Time is UTC+9 and India Standard Time is UTC+5:30. Neither country uses daylight saving, so the gap is a steady three and a half hours all year. Our working day of 9 am to 9 pm IST runs from 12:30 pm to 12:30 am in Japan, seven days a week on WhatsApp.",
      "In practice, most clients in Japan send questions and feedback in the morning, before we start. By 12:30 pm Japan time we are online, have read everything and have replied or started on changes. Calls, reviews and walkthroughs fit comfortably between 1 pm and 6 pm Japan time. Changes requested in the afternoon are usually live on the staging link by the evening, so the next morning starts with progress rather than questions. For launches, migrations or a call with your whole team in the morning, we agree earlier start times in advance.",
    ],
    table: {
      caption: "Japan time compared with India time",
      hide: 2,
      head: ["Japan (JST)", "India (IST)", "What usually happens"],
      rows: [
        ["9:00 am", "5:30 am", "You send feedback or questions; we read them at the start of our day"],
        ["10:00 am", "6:30 am", "Earliest time for a morning call, arranged in advance"],
        ["12:30 pm", "9:00 am", "We are online on WhatsApp, email and calls"],
        ["1:00 pm to 6:00 pm", "9:30 am to 2:30 pm", "Best window for calls, demos and review sessions"],
        ["6:00 pm to 10:00 pm", "2:30 pm to 6:30 pm", "Changes from the day's feedback go live on staging"],
        ["12:30 am", "9:00 pm", "End of our day; urgent issues handled as agreed"],
      ],
    },
  },
  {
    id: "payments",
    heading: "How you pay us: USD, JPY, Wise and bank wire",
    paragraphs: [
      `We quote clients in Japan in US dollars, using the starting prices on this page, with approximate yen figures at ¥${JPY_PER_USD} per dollar for comparison. If your finance team prefers yen, we issue the invoice in JPY at a rate fixed in the quote, so the amount is settled before work starts. Payment is by Wise or international bank wire. Wise is usually cheaper and faster for transfers from Japanese bank accounts, with fees and exchange rates shown before you send.`,
      "Payments are staged against visible milestones rather than taken in full upfront. A typical structure is a part advance to start, a part when the design is approved, and the balance before launch, with the exact split written into the quote. In Japanese terms, builds work like a fixed-scope contract with a defined deliverable, while monthly SEO and maintenance work like an ongoing service agreement that can be stopped with notice. The five free months of maintenance after launch cost nothing and do not lock you into a paid plan.",
      "Some Japanese companies ask whether withholding tax applies to payments to an overseas provider. That depends on whether a payment is treated as a service fee or as a royalty, and on the tax treaty between Japan and India, so your tax accountant should confirm it before the first payment. We provide clear invoices and company details to support that check.",
      "Third-party costs are paid by you directly to the provider: domain registration and renewal, hosting or cloud usage, Shopify or other platform subscriptions, paid themes and apps, LINE plans, email services and payment fees. We list the expected running costs in the quote so your total cost of ownership is clear from the start. Keeping these accounts in your company's name is also what guarantees you own everything.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "buying-guide",
    heading: "How to hire an offshore web developer from Japan",
    paragraphs: [
      "Offshore development has a mixed reputation in Japan. Projects fail for predictable reasons: requirements that were never written down, handing everything over and waiting for the result, no bilingual person on the client side, the person selling is not the person building, no access to work in progress, and nobody reachable after the final payment. Large offshore firms solve the language problem with a bridge engineer; small projects rarely have one. A short checklist avoids most of the risk. Use it with anyone you consider, including us.",
    ],
    list: [
      "<strong>Ask who will build it, by name.</strong> Then ask whether any part will be subcontracted. If you cannot speak to the developer before signing, expect to struggle to reach them later.",
      "<strong>Decide who bridges the language gap.</strong> If your team works in Japanese, name one bilingual colleague or translator who reviews the scope and relays feedback.",
      "<strong>Insist on a written scope.</strong> Pages, features, integrations, languages, revisions, who writes Japanese content, what SEO setup includes, and what is explicitly excluded.",
      "<strong>Test live work, not screenshots.</strong> Open their live sites on your phone over mobile data and run them through Google PageSpeed Insights. Check whether the forms work.",
      "<strong>Keep every account in your name.</strong> Domain, hosting, Shopify, payment providers, LINE Official Account, Google Search Console and analytics must belong to your company, with logins handed over.",
      "<strong>Ask for a staging link from week one.</strong> You should see real progress throughout, not a big reveal at the end.",
      "<strong>Agree the hours overlap.</strong> Ask exactly when they are online in Japan time and how fast they respond. Get it in writing.",
      "<strong>Stage payments against milestones.</strong> Advance, design approval and pre-launch balance is a fair structure. Full payment upfront is a warning sign.",
      "<strong>Clarify ownership and defects.</strong> The contract should say that the code, designs and content created for you are yours once paid, how defects found after delivery are fixed, and that fonts, images and plugins are properly licensed.",
      "<strong>Ask about personal data.</strong> Who will have access to your customer data, where it will be stored, and how the APPI's rules on foreign third parties are handled.",
    ],
    after: [
      "<strong>Red flags worth walking away from:</strong> guaranteed first-page rankings; a domain or hosting account registered in the developer's name; a quote without a scope; pirated or nulled premium themes, which often carry malware; reviews or client logos that cannot be verified; claims of a Japan office that turn out to be a virtual address; and pressure to decide quickly because a discount is about to expire.",
      "<strong>When a Japanese agency is the better choice:</strong> if you need meetings in Japanese, in-person workshops, a vendor who writes your Japanese copy, on-site photography and video bundled with the build, or a registered provider for subsidy funding, a Japanese agency will suit you better, and we will tell you so.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "hosting",
    heading: "Hosting, speed, email and domains for websites in Japan",
    paragraphs: [
      "Japan has excellent cloud infrastructure. AWS, Google Cloud and Microsoft Azure all run regions in Tokyo and Osaka, and every major CDN has edge locations across Japan. Static sites are served from a CDN close to your visitors; apps with databases go into a Tokyo region, with backups in Osaka so that an earthquake or regional outage does not take your data with it. Popular Japanese hosts such as Xserver and Sakura Internet are also fine for WordPress sites, and we work with whichever you already use.",
      "Speed matters because Japanese mobile users are used to fast, well-built apps and sites. Google's Core Web Vitals targets are a Largest Contentful Paint within 2.5 seconds, Interaction to Next Paint within 200 milliseconds and Cumulative Layout Shift below 0.1. We meet them with static HTML where possible, correctly sized modern image formats, system or subset Japanese fonts, lazy-loaded media and very few third-party scripts. We test on mid-range phones with throttled connections, not only on office fibre.",
      "<strong>Email that arrives.</strong> Contact form confirmations and order emails sent to Japanese mobile carrier addresses, such as docomo, au and SoftBank, are often filtered if the sending domain is not properly authenticated. Gmail and Yahoo also tightened their requirements for bulk senders. We set up SPF, DKIM and DMARC for your domain and send transactional email through a reputable provider so messages reach the inbox.",
      "<strong>Domains.</strong> A .jp or .co.jp address is a strong local signal to Japanese customers and to search engines. A .jp domain requires a postal address in Japan, and .co.jp is limited to companies registered in Japan, one per company, so the domain is registered in your company's name. We handle DNS, email records and SSL. City domains such as .tokyo and .osaka are also available. If you also sell internationally, a .com with separate language paths works well, and registering both protects your name for a small yearly cost.",
    ],
  },
];

const tocExtra = [
  { id: "pricing-heading", heading: "Starting prices in USD and yen" },
  { id: "regions-heading", heading: "Region-by-region table" },
  { id: "industries-heading", heading: "Industries" },
  { id: "why-heading", heading: "Comparison" },
  { id: "process-heading", heading: "Process and timelines" },
  { id: "faq-heading", heading: "FAQs" },
];

// ---------- Region table ----------

const regionsHeading = `Japan region by region: what businesses need online in all ${prefectureCount} prefectures`;
const regionsNote = "A quick reference for the patterns described in the guide above. We serve every prefecture remotely from India; none of these are office locations.";
const regionHead = ["Region", "Prefectures", "Business character", "What we usually build"];
const regionHide = [1, 2];
const regionTable = japanRegions.map((r) => [r.name, r.prefectures.join(", "), r.character, r.build]);

// ---------- Industries ----------

const industriesHeading = "What we build for Japan's main industries";
const industries = [
  { name: "Manufacturing and parts suppliers", need: "Specifications, certifications, capacity, lead times and a named contact, in Japanese and English", build: "Searchable catalogues, quotation forms that accept drawings, English export pages, recruitment sites" },
  { name: "Hotels, ryokan and tourism", need: "Photos, prices, access, house rules and booking in their own language", build: "Multilingual sites, booking engine integration, structured data, direct booking offers" },
  { name: "Restaurants and food producers", need: "Menus, reservations, allergens, gift sets and seasonal products", build: "Menu and reservation pages, food ecommerce with cool delivery and noshi, LINE reminders" },
  { name: "Retail and D2C brands", need: "Real product photos, stock, delivery dates and familiar payment methods", build: "Shopify or custom stores with JCB, konbini and PayPay, marketplace stock sync, cross-border stores" },
  { name: "Real estate", need: "Listings by station and area, clear costs, and for foreign buyers, English guidance", build: "Property search, station and area pages, enquiry routing, English pages for international clients" },
  { name: "Education and language schools", need: "Courses, schedules, fees, visa information and trial lessons", build: "Course pages, trial booking, multilingual content for international students, LINE follow-up" },
  { name: "Clinics, dental and beauty", need: "Qualified staff, treatment explanations, hours and easy appointments", build: "Guideline-aware treatment pages, supervisor profiles, appointment booking, LINE reminders" },
  { name: "Professional services", need: "Credentials, practice areas, fees where possible and a discreet way to enquire", build: "Restrained bilingual sites, service pages, secure document upload, articles" },
  { name: "Technology and startups", need: "A site the team can change weekly, docs, pricing pages and trustworthy analytics", build: "Astro or Next.js with a headless CMS, docs, analytics, and often the first product version" },
  { name: "Logistics and trading", need: "Routes, service levels, cut-off times and quick quotes", build: "Quote request tools, tracking pages, B2B ordering portals, AI-OCR for FAX orders" },
];

// ---------- Comparison ----------

const comparisonHeading = "Japanese agency, crowdsourcing freelancer or BtechWaleTech";
const comparisonNote = "Each option suits different projects. This is how they usually differ, so you can choose with open eyes.";
const compHead = ["Typical Japanese agency", "Crowdsourcing freelancer", "BtechWaleTech"];
const comparison = [
  ["Starting price", "Typically ¥150,000 to ¥650,000 for a small corporate site", "Lower, but scope and quality vary widely", `From ${both("Static")}, itemised quote`],
  ["Who does the work", "Director and designers, parts often subcontracted", "One person from a platform such as Lancers or CrowdWorks", "The three engineers you talk to"],
  ["Language", "Japanese", "Usually Japanese", "English; Japanese text from your team or translator"],
  ["Meeting in person", "Yes", "Rarely", "No: remote only, video calls and staging link"],
  ["Hours in Japan time", "Weekday office hours", "Depends on the person", "12:30 pm to 12:30 am JST, 7 days on WhatsApp"],
  ["Subsidy eligibility", "Possible if a registered provider", "Usually not", "Not registered, not eligible"],
  ["SEO setup", "Often a separate contract from ¥100,000 a month", "Frequently skipped", "Titles, schema and sitemap in every build"],
  ["After launch", "Paid maintenance, often ¥20,000 to ¥50,000 a month", "Hard to reach once paid", "5 months of maintenance free"],
  ["Ownership of accounts and code", "Varies; server or CMS sometimes held by agency", "Sometimes held back", "Everything in your company's name"],
];

// ---------- Process ----------

const process = [
  ["Talk", "A short WhatsApp chat or video call in English about your business, customers, competitors and budget. No charge."],
  ["Scope & quote", "Pages, features, languages, integrations, timeline and an itemised USD or JPY quote in writing."],
  ["Design", "Sitemap and wireframes first, then visual design for key pages, reviewed on your own phone."],
  ["Build on staging", "The site is built on a private staging link you can open any time. Afternoon feedback usually lands the same evening."],
  ["Test & SEO", "Payments, forms, Japanese text, legal pages, redirects, speed, schema and sitemap checked end to end."],
  ["Launch & support", "Domain connected, Search Console set up, logins handed over, then 5 months of free maintenance."],
];

// ---------- Related links ----------

const relatedHeading = "Websites, apps, AI automation, SEO and software for businesses across Japan";
const related = [
  { name: "Website developer in Japan", href: "/japan/website-developer/" },
  { name: "AI automation engineer in Japan", href: "/japan/ai-automation-engineer/" },
  { name: "Android & iOS app developer in Japan", href: "/japan/android-ios-developer/" },
  { name: "SEO services in Japan", href: "/japan/seo-services/" },
  { name: "Software development in Japan", href: "/japan/software-development/" },
];

const processHeading = "From first message to a live site";
const quoteFoot = `All figures are starting prices in USD (about ¥${JPY_PER_USD} per dollar for comparison); your quote depends on requirements. 5 months maintenance free after launch.`;
const timelineFine = "Timelines assume content, translations and approvals arrive on time. Payments, languages and user accounts add testing time to ecommerce and custom builds.";
const closingHeading = "Tell us about your project in Japan";
const closingNote = "Send a few lines in English on WhatsApp about your business and what you need. You get questions first, then a page plan, a timeline and an itemised quote in USD or JPY, usually within two working days. Nothing is billed until you approve the scope.";

// ---------- Structured data ----------

const regionsServed = japanRegions.flatMap((r) => r.prefectures).map((p) => (p === "Tokyo" ? "Tokyo Metropolis" : p === "Hokkaido" ? p : `${p} Prefecture`));
const citiesServed = [...cityRows.map(([city]) => city.replace(" (23 wards)", "")), "Naha", "Kanazawa", "Kagoshima", "Matsuyama", "Takamatsu", "Nagasaki"];
const country = { "@type": "Country", name: countryName };

const baseService = countryServiceSchema({ path, description: page.description, country: countryName, cities: citiesServed });
const professionalServiceSchema = {
  ...baseService,
  "@id": `${url}#service`,
  currenciesAccepted: "USD, JPY",
  paymentAccepted: "Wise, Bank wire",
  areaServed: [
    country,
    ...regionsServed.map((name) => ({ "@type": "State", name, containedInPlace: country })),
    ...citiesServed.map((name) => ({ "@type": "City", name, containedInPlace: country })),
  ],
};

const webPageSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "@id": `${url}#webpage`,
  url,
  name: page.title,
  description: page.description,
  inLanguage: "en-JP",
  about: { "@id": `${url}#service` },
  speakable: { "@type": "SpeakableSpecification", cssSelector: ["#quick-answer", "h1"] },
};
---

<BaseLayout meta={page} schema={[webPageSchema, professionalServiceSchema, breadcrumbListSchema(page.breadcrumbs), faqSchema(faqs)]}>

  <!-- ===================== HERO ===================== -->
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="country-heading">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <ol>
            {page.breadcrumbs.map((b, i) => (
              <li>{i + 1 === page.breadcrumbs.length ? <span aria-current="page">{b.label}</span> : <a href={b.href}>{b.label}</a>}</li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </nav>
        <p class="eyebrow">{heroEyebrow}</p>
        <h1 id="country-heading">{page.h1}</h1>
        <p class="lede">{page.intro}</p>
        <ul class="facts" aria-label="Quick facts">
          {facts.map(([label, value]) => <li><strong>{label}</strong><span>{value}</span></li>)}
        </ul>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn-primary" href={siteContact.whatsappHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span>WhatsApp for a free quote</span>
            <span class="btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
          <a class="btn-ghost" href={siteContact.emailHref}>Email {siteContact.email}</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="hero-pills" aria-label="What we build">
          {pills.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="hero-origin">
          <span class="origin-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {heroOrigin}
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="quote-card" aria-label={`Starting prices for ${countryName}`}>
        <p class="quote-kicker">{countryName} starting prices</p>
        <ul class="quote-rows">
          {priceRows.slice(0, 5).map((r) => (
            <li><span>{r.service}</span><strong><small>from </small>{r.usd}</strong></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="quote-foot">{quoteFoot}</p>
        <a class="btn-primary btn-block" href={siteContact.whatsappHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <span>Get my quote on WhatsApp</span><span class="btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== STATS ===================== -->
  <section class="stats-section" aria-label="BtechWaleTech in numbers">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <ul class="stat-band">
        {stats.map((s) => (
          <li><span class="stat-num">{s.value}</span><span class="stat-label">{s.label}</span></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== QUICK ANSWER + SNAPSHOT ===================== -->
  <section class="answer" aria-labelledby="answer-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap answer-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The short answer</p>
        <h2 id="answer-heading">{answerHeading}</h2>
        <p id="quick-answer" class="answer-text">{quickAnswer}</p>
        <p class="answer-more">{answerMore}</p>
      </div>
      <table class="snapshot">
        <caption>{countryName} at a glance</caption>
        <tbody>
          {snapshot.map((row) => (
            <tr><th scope="row">{row.label}</th><td>{row.value}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== SERVICES ===================== -->
  <section class="services" aria-labelledby="services-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Services</p>
        <h2 id="services-heading">{servicesHeading}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="bento">
        {services.map((s) => {
          const inner = (
            <div class="card-core">
              <h3>{s.name}</h3>
              <p>{s.note}</p>
              {"href" in s && <span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>}
            </div>
          );
          return "href" in s ? <a class={`card card-${s.size}`} href={s.href}>{inner}</a> : <div class={`card card-${s.size}`}>{inner}</div>;
        })}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== PRICING ===================== -->
  <section class="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h2 id="pricing-heading">{pricingHeading}</h2>
        <p class="section-note">{pricingIntro}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="price-table fit-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">Starts from</th><th scope="col">About in yen</th><th scope="col" class="hide-sm">Typical timeline</th><th scope="col" class="hide-sm">What is included</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {priceRows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{r.service}</th>
                <td class="price">{r.usd}</td>
                <td class="price">{jpy(r.service)}</td>
                <td class="hide-sm">{r.timeline}</td>
                <td class="hide-sm">{r.includes}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">{pricingFine} See the <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> for full scope guidance.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== LONG-FORM GUIDE ===================== -->
  <section class="guide" aria-label={`Guide to web development for ${countryName}`}>
    <div class="section-wrap guide-grid">
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <p class="toc-title">On this page</p>
        <ol>
          {guide.map((g) => <li><a href={`#${g.id}`}>{g.heading}</a></li>)}
          {tocExtra.map((t) => <li><a href={`#${t.id}`}>{t.heading}</a></li>)}
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <div class="prose">
        {guide.map((g) => (
          <article aria-labelledby={g.id}>
            <h2 id={g.id}>{g.heading}</h2>
            {g.paragraphs.map((p) => <p set:html={p} />)}
            {g.list && <ul>{g.list.map((li) => <li set:html={li} />)}</ul>}
            {g.blocks && g.blocks.map((b) => (
              <div class="state-block">
                <h3>{b.name}</h3>
                <p>{b.text}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
            {g.table && (
              <div class="comparison-table-wrap prose-table">
                <table class="price-table fit-sm">
                  <caption class="sr-only">{g.table.caption}</caption>
                  <thead><tr>{g.table.head.map((h, i) => <th scope="col" class={i === g.table!.hide ? "hide-sm" : undefined}>{h}</th>)}</tr></thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {g.table.rows.map((row) => (
                      <tr>{row.map((cell, i) => (i === 0 ? <th scope="row">{cell}</th> : <td class={i === g.table!.hide ? "hide-sm" : undefined}>{cell}</td>))}</tr>
                    ))}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            )}
            {g.after && g.after.map((p) => <p set:html={p} />)}
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== REGION TABLE ===================== -->
  <section class="industries" aria-labelledby="regions-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Coverage</p>
        <h2 id="regions-heading">{regionsHeading}</h2>
        <p class="section-note">{regionsNote}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="price-table fit-sm">
          <thead><tr>{regionHead.map((h, i) => <th scope="col" class={regionHide.includes(i) ? "hide-sm" : undefined}>{h}</th>)}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {regionTable.map((row) => (
              <tr>{row.map((cell, i) => (i === 0 ? <th scope="row">{cell}</th> : <td class={regionHide.includes(i) ? "hide-sm" : undefined}>{cell}</td>))}</tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== INDUSTRIES ===================== -->
  <section class="industries" aria-labelledby="industries-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Industries</p>
        <h2 id="industries-heading">{industriesHeading}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="price-table fit-sm">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Industry</th><th scope="col" class="hide-sm">What buyers look for</th><th scope="col">What we build</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {industries.map((i) => (
              <tr><th scope="row">{i.name}</th><td class="hide-sm">{i.need}</td><td>{i.build}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== COMPARISON ===================== -->
  <section class="advantage" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Compare</p>
        <h2 id="why-heading">{comparisonHeading}</h2>
        <p class="section-note">{comparisonNote}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="comparison-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">What matters</th>
              <th scope="col" class="col-other">{compHead[0]}</th>
              <th scope="col" class="col-other">{compHead[1]}</th>
              <th scope="col" class="col-us">{compHead[2]}</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {comparison.map(([aspect, agency, cheap, us]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" class="td-aspect">{aspect}</th>
                <td class="col-other">{agency}</td>
                <td class="col-other">{cheap}</td>
                <td class="td-us"><span class="td-us-inner"><span class="td-check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>{us}</span></td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== PROCESS ===================== -->
  <section class="process" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2 id="process-heading">{processHeading}</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps steps-six">
        {process.map(([step, detail], i) => (
          <li><span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span><h3>{step}</h3><p>{detail}</p></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <div class="comparison-table-wrap timeline-wrap">
        <table class="price-table fit-sm">
          <caption class="sr-only">Typical project timelines</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Project</th><th scope="col">Typical timeline</th><th scope="col" class="hide-sm">What it covers</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {pricingPlans.map((plan) => (
              <tr><th scope="row">{plan.name}</th><td>{plan.timeline}</td><td class="hide-sm">{plan.summary}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">{timelineFine}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== FAQ ===================== -->
  <section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
        <h2 id="faq-heading">{countryName} web development questions, answered</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary><span>{f.question}</span><span class="faq-mark" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
            <p>{f.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== RELATED ===================== -->
  <section class="locations" aria-labelledby="related-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Services in Japan</p>
        <h2 id="related-heading">{relatedHeading}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="city-cloud">
        {related.map((c) => <a class="city-chip" href={c.href}>{c.name}</a>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== CLOSING CTA ===================== -->
  <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <div class="closing-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">Next step</p>
        <h2 id="cta-heading">{closingHeading}</h2>
        <p class="closing-note">{closingNote}</p>
        <div class="hero-actions closing-actions">
          <a class="btn-primary" href={siteContact.whatsappHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span>WhatsApp us</span><span class="btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
          <a class="btn-ghost" href={siteContact.emailHref}>{siteContact.email}</a>
        </div>
        <p class="closing-links">
          <a href="/services/">All services</a> · <a href="/services/web-development/">Web development</a> · <a href="/services/seo-services/">SEO services</a> ·
          <a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a> · <a href="/portfolio/">Portfolio</a> · <a href="/about/">About</a> · <a href="/countries/">Countries</a> · <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Tokens and section styles mirror src/pages/[city].astro so country pages match the city pages. */
  :root {
    --paper: #FDFCFB;
    --surface: #F8F9FA;
    --surface-low: #F3F4F5;
    --midnight: #0F172A;
    --slate: #334155;
    --slate-muted: #64748B;
    --gold: #D4AF37;
    --gold-muted: #C5A059;
    --hairline: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.10);
    --ease: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
    --font: 'Hanken Grotesk', system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
  }
  :global(body) { background: var(--paper); color: var(--midnight); }

  h1, h2, h3 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font); color: var(--midnight); letter-spacing: -0.02em; font-weight: 700; }
  p { margin: 0; }
  section { scroll-margin-top: 5rem; }
  .sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }

  .section-wrap { max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 clamp(1rem, 5vw, 5rem); }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.65rem; margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--gold-muted); font-family: var(--font); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .eyebrow::before { width: 1.75rem; height: 1px; background: var(--gold-muted); content: ""; flex-shrink: 0; }

  .section-head { max-width: 48rem; margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .section-head h2 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.6rem); line-height: 1.15; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .section-note { color: var(--slate); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .section-note a, .fine a { color: var(--midnight); text-decoration-color: var(--gold); text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  /* Buttons */
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.85rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .btn-primary, .btn-ghost {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; min-height: 3.1rem; padding: 0 1.6rem;
    border-radius: 2px; font-family: var(--font); font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 250ms var(--ease); max-width: 100%; overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--midnight); color: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--midnight); }
  .btn-primary:hover { background: #1E293B; transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .btn-arrow { color: var(--gold); transition: transform 250ms var(--ease); }
  .btn-primary:hover .btn-arrow { transform: translateX(3px); }
  .btn-ghost { color: var(--midnight); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); background: transparent; }
  .btn-ghost:hover { border-color: var(--gold); }
  .btn-block { width: 100%; justify-content: center; }

  /* Hero */
  .hero { padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem) 0 clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .hero-inner {
    max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 clamp(1rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(0, 0.85fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem); align-items: center;
  }
  .crumbs ol { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--slate-muted); }
  .crumbs li + li::before { content: "/"; margin-right: 0.4rem; color: var(--hairline); }
  .crumbs a { color: var(--slate-muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--midnight); }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4vw, 3.25rem); line-height: 1.12; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 100%; overflow-wrap: anywhere; text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lede { color: var(--slate); font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.3vw, 1.1rem); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 38rem; }
  .facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 12rem), 1fr)); gap: 0.6rem; max-width: 46rem; margin: 1.6rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .facts li { display: grid; gap: 0.2rem; padding: 0.75rem 0.95rem; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 4px; background: #fff; }
  .facts strong { color: var(--gold-muted); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .facts span { color: var(--midnight); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .hero-pills { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 0; padding: 1.5rem 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); list-style: none; }
  .hero-pills li { padding: 0.35rem 0.8rem; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 2px; color: var(--slate); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .hero-origin { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; color: var(--slate-muted); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .origin-dot { width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--gold); flex-shrink: 0; }

  .quote-card {
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem); background: var(--midnight); color: #F8F9FA; border-radius: 4px;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 50px -20px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.45);
  }
  .quote-kicker { color: var(--gold); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .quote-rows { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .quote-rows li { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 0.8rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); font-size: 0.92rem; color: #CBD5E1; }
  .quote-rows strong { color: #fff; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
  .quote-rows small { color: #94A3B8; font-weight: 400; }
  .quote-foot { font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #94A3B8; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .quote-card .btn-primary { background: var(--gold); color: var(--midnight); border-color: var(--gold); }
  .quote-card .btn-primary .btn-arrow { color: var(--midnight); }

  /* Stats */
  .stats-section { padding: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem) 0; background: var(--midnight); }
  .stat-band { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1px; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06); }
  .stat-band li { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; text-align: center; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem) 1rem; background: var(--midnight); min-width: 0; }
  .stat-num { color: #F8F9FA; font-family: var(--font); font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .stat-label { color: #94A3B8; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.4; max-width: 12rem; }

  /* Quick answer */
  .answer { padding: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem) 0; }
  .answer-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem); align-items: start; }
  .answer h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.25rem); line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .answer-text { font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--slate); padding-left: 1.1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); }
  .answer-more { margin-top: 1.1rem; color: var(--slate); line-height: 1.75; }
  .snapshot { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .snapshot caption { text-align: left; padding: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--slate-muted); }
  .snapshot th, .snapshot td { padding: 0.8rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; line-height: 1.5; }
  .snapshot th { width: 38%; background: var(--surface-low); font-weight: 600; }
  .snapshot td { color: var(--slate); }

  /* Services bento */
  .services { padding: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem) 0; background: var(--surface); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .bento { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: var(--hairline); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .card { display: block; background: var(--paper); text-decoration: none; transition: background-color 250ms ease; }
  .card:hover { background: #fff; }
  .card-lg { grid-column: span 2; }
  .card-md { grid-column: span 2; }
  .card-core { position: relative; padding: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.6rem); height: 100%; }
  .card-core h3 { font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; line-height: 1.25; padding-right: 2rem; }
  .card-core p { color: var(--slate); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .card-arrow {
    position: absolute; top: 1.4rem; right: 1.4rem; display: inline-grid; place-items: center; width: 1.75rem; height: 1.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline); color: var(--slate-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; transition: all 250ms var(--ease);
  }
  a.card:hover .card-arrow { background: var(--midnight); border-color: var(--midnight); color: var(--paper); }

  /* Tables */
  .advantage, .pricing, .industries { padding: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .pricing { background: var(--surface); }
  .comparison-table-wrap { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; }
  .comparison-table, .price-table { width: 100%; min-width: 40rem; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; background: var(--paper); }
  .comparison-table thead th, .price-table thead th {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;
    text-align: left; background: var(--surface-low); color: var(--midnight); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .comparison-table thead .col-us { background: var(--midnight); color: var(--gold); }
  .comparison-table tbody tr, .price-table tbody tr { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .comparison-table td, .comparison-table th[scope="row"], .price-table td, .price-table th[scope="row"] { padding: 1rem 1.25rem; vertical-align: top; line-height: 1.5; text-align: left; }
  .td-aspect, .price-table th[scope="row"] { font-weight: 600; color: var(--midnight); }
  td.col-other { color: var(--slate-muted); }
  .td-us { background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.06); }
  .td-us-inner { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; color: var(--midnight); font-weight: 600; }
  .td-check { color: var(--gold-muted); font-weight: 700; }
  .price-table td { color: var(--slate); }
  .price-table .price { color: var(--midnight); font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
  .fine { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--slate-muted); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 54rem; }
  .timeline-wrap { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .prose-table { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .prose-table + p { margin-top: 1.5rem; }

  /* Long-form guide */
  .guide { padding: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .guide-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 15rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem); align-items: start; }
  .toc { position: sticky; top: 6rem; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .toc-title { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--slate-muted); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .toc ol { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; border-left: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .toc a { display: block; padding: 0.4rem 0 0.4rem 1rem; color: var(--slate); text-decoration: none; line-height: 1.4; }
  .toc a:hover { color: var(--midnight); box-shadow: inset 2px 0 0 var(--gold); }
  .prose { max-width: 46rem; min-width: 0; }
  .prose article + article { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 3rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .prose h2 { font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.6vw, 1.9rem); line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; scroll-margin-top: 5rem; }
  .prose h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .prose p { color: var(--slate); font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.85; }
  .prose p + p { margin-top: 1.1rem; }
  .prose ul { margin: 1.1rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; color: var(--slate); line-height: 1.8; }
  .prose ul + p, .prose .state-block + p { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .prose li + li { margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  .prose :global(a) { color: var(--midnight); text-decoration-color: var(--gold); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .prose :global(strong) { color: var(--midnight); }
  .state-block { margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px dashed var(--hairline); }

  /* Locations */
  .locations { padding: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem) 0; background: var(--surface); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .city-cloud { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .city-chip {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 2.6rem; padding: 0 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 2px; color: var(--midnight); background: var(--paper); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 250ms var(--ease);
  }
  .city-chip:hover { border-color: var(--gold); transform: translateY(-2px); }

  /* Process */
  .process { padding: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .steps li { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; align-content: start; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem); background: var(--paper); }
  .steps li + li { border-left: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .step-num { color: var(--gold-muted); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; }
  .steps h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .steps p { color: var(--slate); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .steps-six { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .steps-six li:nth-child(4) { border-left: none; }
  .steps-six li:nth-child(n+4) { border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }

  /* FAQ */
  .faq { padding: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .faq-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .faq-item { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
  .faq-item summary {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem; padding: 1.35rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font); font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.4vw, 1.12rem); font-weight: 600; list-style: none; cursor: pointer;
  }
